 {:seon.task/name "every-tools-answer-says-what-it-is"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner, 2026-11-11: 'Agents need to know that context exists and we need explanations and short instructions that the agent can use to pull in more context'; and on the default printer: '(+ 1 1) ... I want the answer'. What exists, counted: about 55 public tools in my.agent and my.db; four answer a value whose metadata names a schema that declares a model render (the lines of a file, a search that found nothing, a proved test, a merged branch: docs/render.md#how-a-value-is-printed); the rest answer plain values the printer cuts with no word of what was cut or how to get it. Plan: one way. Each tool's answer carries the schema that names it, and that schema's entry holds its description, its model render and what brings more; a plain value from the agent's own form prints plainly, as now. No tool formats a string of its own. Deletes: each tool's own formatting as it is moved. Proof, red first: a law over every public var of the tool namespaces: its contract's answer is a registered schema with a description, or the var is a plain function of values named as such by its metadata; the count of tools outside the law may only fall."
